# Crosshair System

Weapon-state crosshair rendered via IMGUI `OnGUI()` in `View/AimCursorOverlay.cs`.

## Two Cursors

| Cursor | Source | Visual | Purpose |
|--------|--------|--------|---------|
| **Raw** | `player.RawAimPoint` | Small white dot (6px) | Player intent, instant from mouse |
| **Weapon** | `player.WeaponAimPoint` | Crosshair / state indicator | Where weapon actually aims, carries state info |

Raw cursor is always a dot and never changes. Weapon cursor shape/color/animation reflects weapon state.

## Weapon Cursor States

| WeaponPhase | Condition | Visual | Color |
|-------------|-----------|--------|-------|
| `Ready` | `AmmoInMagazine > 0` | 4-line crosshair + center dot | Green `(0.2, 1, 0.3, 0.9)` |
| `Ready` | Empty mag + no reserve | 4-line crosshair + center dot | Red `(1, 0.25, 0.2, 0.9)` |
| `Firing` | Just shot (1 tick) | Crosshair with max bloom gap | White `(1, 1, 1, 0.95)` |
| `Cooldown` | Post-shot delay | Bloom gap contracting back | White->Green lerp |
| `Reloading` | Reload in progress | Ring of 12 dots (no crosshair) | Orange filled / gray empty |
| `Equipping` | Drawing weapon | Crosshair fading in | Green, alpha 0->1 |
| `Unequipping` | Holstering weapon | Crosshair fading out | Green, alpha 1->0 |
| Unarmed | `EquippedWeapon == null` | Single gray dot (15px) | Gray `(0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.6)` |

Rolling (`IsRolling == true`) applies 0.3 alpha multiplier to any state above.

## Crosshair Geometry

All configurable via DevCheats Crosshair section. Top line fades out during ADS.

## ADS Crosshair

Gap/bloom lerp toward ADS values (`AdsBaseGap`, `AdsBloomExtraGap`). Top line fades (`alpha *= 1 - adsBlend`).

## Bloom Animation

Triggered by Firing->Cooldown. Gap starts expanded, contracts to base via SmoothStep.

## Reload Ring

12 dots in circle (radius 42px), from 12 o'clock clockwise. Filled = orange, empty = gray.

## Recoil

Subtract-apply pattern in AimingSystem. ADS reduces recoil kick and boosts recovery.
See `docs/ai/weapons.md` for recoil details and per-weapon stats.

## Hit Marker System

COD-style X-markers driven by `HitConfirmed` events from `DamageSystem`.

### HitMarker Struct

```
struct HitMarker {
    float time;              // Time.time when created
    bool isKill;             // target died
    bool isHeadshot;         // headshot
    float absorptionRatio;   // 0=full pen, 1=full absorption
    bool isRicochet;         // helmet ricochet
}
```

### Marker Types

- **Regular hit**: white X, `HitDuration` (0.3s), `HitLineLength` (14px)
- **Kill**: red X, `KillDuration` (0.5s), `KillLineLength` (18px), color `(1, 0.15, 0.15)`
- **Headshot**: gold double-X (inner + outer at `HeadshotOuterScale` 1.25x), `HeadshotDuration` (0.5s), color `(1, 0.85, 0.2)`
- **Ricochet**: blue spark X at 50% length, 60% gap, 80% thickness, `RicochetDuration` (0.2s), color `(0.5, 0.7, 1)`

### Proportional Sizing (Armor Absorption)

- Size: `absScale = 1 - absorptionRatio * 0.5` (1.0 at full pen, 0.5 at full absorption)
- Color: regular hits lerp `HitColor -> ArmorHitColor` by `absorptionRatio`. Kill/headshot colors never blended.
- `ArmorHitColor` default: gray-blue `(0.6, 0.65, 0.7)`

### DevCheats Params

`DevCheatsCrosshairSection`: `HitMarkerScale`, `HitDuration`, `KillDuration`, `HeadshotDuration`, `RicochetDuration`, `HitLineLength`, `KillLineLength`, `HitGapStart`, `HitGapExpand`, `HitMarkerThickness`, `HitColor`, `KillColor`, `HeadshotColor`, `ArmorHitColor`, `RicochetColor`, `HeadshotOuterScale`, `HeadshotOuterExpandMul`.

